flowchart LR
  accTitle: Graph state references and authoritative records
  accDescr: CognitiveCycleState contains checkpoint-friendly identifiers, versions, flags, and routing values. These references point to separate authoritative repositories for CoALA memory, mechanism state, approvals and actions, observations, and the simulated world. The PostgreSQL checkpoint stores graph continuation state but does not replace those records.
  subgraph STATE[CognitiveCycleState]
    IDS[Execution and scope IDs]
    REFS[Memory, evidence, intention, plan and observation IDs]
    ROUTE[Versions, counters and route decisions]
  end
  CP[(PostgreSQL graph checkpoint)]
  STATE <--> CP
  subgraph STORES[Authoritative owners]
    MEM[(CoALA memory repositories)]
    MECH[(B1 B2 B3 B4 B6 runtime records)]
    AUTH[(Approval and action ledgers)]
    OBS[(Observation and outcome records)]
    WORLD[(Simulated world snapshot)]
  end
  REFS -. identifiers only .-> MEM
  REFS -. identifiers only .-> MECH
  REFS -. identifiers only .-> AUTH
  REFS -. identifiers only .-> OBS
  REFS -. external reference .-> WORLD
  ROUTE --> CP
